{"Non-deterministic hash breaks cache - the cache key uses Python's built-in hash() on a tuple, but Python 3 randomizes hash seeds per-process via PYTHONHASHSEED, causing cache misses across workers and failed invalidation": 0.9230339527130127, "Wrong dataset for upsampling - organization_events_stats._get_event_stats determines upsampling eligibility using the outer-scope dataset, but the query is executed against the scoped_dataset argument which can differ in dashboard split paths": 0.9475026726722717, "No feature flag for upsampling - the new error upsampling feature is gated only by an options-based project allowlist instead of using the repository's standard features.has() feature flag mechanism": 0.5078509449958801, "Factory bypasses sample_rate validation - the test factory sets normalized_data['sample_rate'] directly from contexts.error_sampling.client_sample_rate without production's allowlist and 0<rate<=1 validation": 0.47366079688072205, "Accidental git submodule file committed - a file named sentry-repo containing a git submodule commit pointer was accidentally added to the repository root": 0.9806472063064575, "Test setup overwrites self.user - in OrganizationEventsStatsErrorUpsamplingTest.setUp, self.user is first used to call self.login_as and then immediately overwritten with self.create_user(), causing inconsistency": 0.9217705726623535, "Cache bypassed when value is False - when _are_all_projects_error_upsampled returns False and is cached, adding a project to the allowlist won't take effect for up to 60 seconds due to the cached False value": 0.6656814217567444}